## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, compliant telemetry pipeline with region isolation and real-time processing. It probes data modeling, idempotent semantics, and resilience at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Regional Pub/Sub and Dataflow streaming
- Schema validation and deduplication
- Tenant isolation via separate datasets and buckets
- Data residency and cross-region backups
- Observability and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow transform sketch
function process(event) {
  if (!validateSchema(event)) throw new Error('Invalid');
  if (isDuplicate(event)) return;
  if (isAnomalous(event)) emit('anomaly', event);
  emitAggregates(event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you allocate costs per tenant?
- How would you test end-to-end failover in a CI pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical ability to design region-specific, tenant-isolated data pipelines with proper security, onboarding, and DR considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Regional data residency per tenant
- Streaming ETL with Dataflow
- Idempotency and deduplication
- Tenant lifecycle automation (onboard/offboard)
- Security: CMEK, IAM least privilege
- Observability with Cloud Monitoring/Logging
- Disaster recovery and cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo dedup write to BigQuery per tenant
function writeEvent(evt) {
  const key = evt.tenantId + "_" + evt.eventId;
  if (dedupStore.has(key)) return;
  dedupStore.add(key);
  bigQueryWrite(evt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate idempotency and replay safety in the Dataflow pipeline at scale?
- What would your DR test plan look like for region failover and data residency?
